# Settings in communication

Settings refer to the environmental and contextual factors that shape how communication occurs. Duhigg examines how physical spaces, social dynamics, and situational contexts influence the effectiveness of conversations and interactions.

## Key factors
- Physical environment affects comfort and openness
- Social context determines appropriate communication styles
- Group dynamics shape individual expression
- Trust-building exercises create favorable settings for collaboration

## Connection to existing concepts
- Relates to the [[environment]] mental model
- Connects to [[building-a-cohesive-team]] through trust and shared goals
- Overlaps with [[communication-skills]] as a contextual dimension
